# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: iderunboardsave
# board: discover
# A program is kept on a board from the editor, and is there afterwards.
#
# Save on <board> puts the file in the interpreter's own named slot, and
# the board shows that slot in its namespace as /data/<name>.bas -- which
# is where this reads it back, through the shell's own mount, so the
# proof is the same road a person would take to find it.
wait 60
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title Open
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title Open
click-window Project
wait 8
note the row the list stands on is quiet.bas, the one to keep
key Down
wait 6
key Down
wait 8
note where runs go is chosen once, in Connect; the project remembers it
click 175 8
wait 8
menu-pick nrf54lm20b
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Save on nrf54lm20b
menu-pick Save on nrf54lm20b
wait 250
note kept under the file's own name, and readable where the board put it
expect-read /devices/nrf54lm20b/data/quiet.bas KEPT
quit
